<%# Terms of use and sale, the English translation. %>
<section>
  <h2>1. Purpose</h2>
  <p>These terms of use and sale (the "Terms") govern access to and use of Fitora, an online management software for gyms, studios and clubs (the "Service"), and the purchase of its paid plans. Creating an account or using the Service means accepting the Terms.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>2. Publisher</h2>
  <p>The Service is published by <%= legal_identity(tax_label: "tax ID") %>. Contact: <a href="mailto:<%= legal_contact %>"><%= legal_contact %></a><% if issuer.phone.present? %>, <%= issuer.phone %><% end %>.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>3. Definitions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Customer</strong>: the person or business that runs one or more gyms and opens an administrator account.</li>
    <li><strong>User</strong>: anyone who signs in to the Service on the Customer's behalf (administrator, front desk, coach).</li>
    <li><strong>Member</strong>: a member of the Customer's gym, whose details the Customer records, and who may be given access to the member app.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>4. Account and free trial</h2>
  <p>The Customer opens an account online and confirms their email address. The first <%= Subscription::TRIAL_DAYS %> days are free, with no commitment and no payment method. When the trial ends, access is suspended until a plan is chosen; the data is kept.</p>
  <p>The Customer is responsible for their Users' credentials and for what is done with them. They create their team's access and give each the appropriate role.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>5. Plans and prices</h2>
  <p>Fitora comes in two plans, Starter and Pro, described on the website and in the account's "Fitora subscription" page, paid monthly or yearly. Prices are shown before tax; the invoice adds the VAT and stamp duty in force. Fitora may change its prices; a new price applies from the next period, after the Customer has been told.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>6. Invoicing, payment and suspension</h2>
  <p>Each period is invoiced by Fitora to the Customer. The Customer has <%= Subscription::GRACE_DAYS %> days after the end of the paid period to pay for the next one. After that, access to the Service is suspended until payment; no data is deleted because of the suspension. Amounts paid are not refundable, unless Fitora failed to meet its obligations.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>7. The Customer's commitments</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Use the Service lawfully and in accordance with these Terms.</li>
    <li>Enter accurate information, and record about Members only what is needed to manage their membership.</li>
    <li>Tell Members how their data is processed and obtain their explicit consent where the law requires it, in particular for health information and photos.</li>
    <li>Not attempt to reach another gym's data, nor disrupt the Service.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>8. Members' data</h2>
  <p>The Customer remains the controller of their Members' data; Fitora processes it on the Customer's behalf, only to provide the Service, and never sells or transfers it. The details are in the <a href="/confidentialite">privacy policy</a>.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>9. Availability and support</h2>
  <p>Fitora takes reasonable steps to keep the Service available around the clock, except for maintenance, a supplier's incident or force majeure. The Customer can reach support from their account (Support). Data is backed up every day.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>10. Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>The Service, its code, texts and graphics belong to the publisher. The Customer receives a personal, non-exclusive right to use it for the length of their subscription. The data the Customer enters remains theirs.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>11. Liability</h2>
  <p>Fitora is bound by an obligation of means. It is not liable for indirect damage (loss of revenue, of customers…), nor for decisions the Customer takes from the Service's information. In any event, Fitora's liability is limited to the amounts the Customer paid over the last twelve months.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>12. Term, termination and getting the data back</h2>
  <p>The subscription runs period by period (month or year) for as long as the Customer pays for it. The Customer may stop at any time; the current period remains due. Before leaving, they can export their members and data (Settings → Import / Export). On request, Fitora deletes the account and its data, except what it must keep by law (accounting records in particular).</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>13. Changes to the Terms</h2>
  <p>Fitora may change the Terms; the new version is published on this page and the Customer is told. Using the Service after it takes effect means accepting it.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>14. Governing law and disputes</h2>
  <p>The Terms are governed by Tunisian law. Failing an amicable settlement, any dispute falls under the competent courts of Tunis.</p>
</section>
